The '''1979 NFL draft''' was the procedure by which [[National Football League]] teams selected amateur [[college football]] players. It is officially known as the NFL Annual Player Selection Meeting. The [[NFL draft|draft]] was held May 3–4, [[1979 NFL season|1979]], at the [[Waldorf Astoria New York|Waldorf Astoria Hotel]] in [[New York City]], New York.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.footballgeography.com/nfl-draft-sites/ |title=NFL Draft Locations |author=<!--Staff writer(s); no by-line.--> |date=October 2, 2014 |website=FootballGeography.com |access-date=October 23, 2014 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150905090250/http://www.footballgeography.com/nfl-draft-sites/ |archive-date=September 5, 2015 |url-status=dead }}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Salomone |first1=Dan |title=NFL Draft headed to Chicago in 2015 |url=http://www.giants.com/news-and-blogs/article-1/NFL-Draft-headed-to-Chicago-in-2015/3ac322b1-3b4c-4a16-aba7-6e08d31b1756 |access-date=June 3, 2015 |publisher=[[New York Giants]] |work=Giants.com |date=October 2, 2014 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150930065327/http://www.giants.com/news-and-blogs/article-1/NFL-Draft-headed-to-Chicago-in-2015/3ac322b1-3b4c-4a16-aba7-6e08d31b1756 |archive-date=September 30, 2015 |url-status=dead }}</ref> The league also held a [[NFL draft#Supplemental draft|supplemental draft]] after the regular draft and before the regular season.

The [[Buffalo Bills]] held the [[List of first overall National Football League Draft picks|first overall pick]] in the draft, acquired from the [[San Francisco 49ers]] in the trade which sent [[O. J. Simpson]] to his hometown team. The Bills' selection at No. 1, [[Ohio State Buckeyes football|Ohio State]] linebacker [[Tom Cousineau]], refused to sign with the Bills and instead signed a lucrative deal with the [[Montreal Alouettes]] of the [[Canadian Football League]].

